1
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
A new era must commence

2
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Bionicle: The Legend Reborn is a action, adventure,
animation film directed by Mark Baldo.

3
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Once the ruler of an entire universe, the Great Spirit Mata Nui finds himself cast out of his own
body, his spirit trapped inside the fabled Mask of Life, hurtling through space.

4
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
After landing on the far-away planet of Bara Magna, the mask creates a new body for Mata Nui, who
unwillingly gets caught up in the furious battles of the nearly barren and dangerous planet.

5
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Skrall / Bone Hunters / Vorox (voice), played by Dee Bradley Baker.

6
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Strakk / Tarix (voice), played by Jeff Bennett.

7
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Ackar (voice), played by Jim Cummings.

8
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Mata Nui (voice), played by Michael Dorn.

9
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Gresh (voice), played by Mark Famiglietti.

10
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Metus (voice), played by David Leisure.

11
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Bionicle: The Legend Reborn is a 2009 animated science fantasy
action film based on the Bionicle toy line by Lego.

12
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
It is the fourth and final Bionicle film to be released.

13
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
Distributed by Universal Studios Home Entertainment, the film is a stand-alone sequel to the trilogy of
films released by Buena Vista Home Entertainment under the Miramax Home Entertainment label.

14
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
It follows the toy line's 2009 story and features a different set
of characters than that of the first three films.

15
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
The Legend Reborn was released on September 15, 2009, in the United States and
Canada, October 5 in the United Kingdom, and September 2 in Australia.

16
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
The film stars Michael Dorn as the voice of Mata Nui.

17
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
The Legend Reborn was intended to be the start of a trilogy of films, but production on the
sequels was cancelled due to Lego discontinuing the release of Bionicle toys in 2010.

18
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
The story was concluded through other media outlets, including comic
books and a web story titled the "Mata Nui Saga".

19
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
The tone is thought_provoking.
